  "question": {
    "text": "A <math> <mrow> <mn>100</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>W</mtext></mrow> </math> sodium lamp radiates energy uniformly in all directions. The wavelength of the sodium light is <math> <mrow> <mn>589</mn><mtext>&nbsp;nm</mtext></mrow></math>. What is the energy per photon in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>)</mo></math> associated with the sodium light? [ <math>&nbsp;<mrow><mtext>h&nbsp;=&nbsp;6</mtext><msup> <mrow> <mtext>.63&nbsp;×&nbsp;10</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>-34</mtext></mrow> </msup> <mtext>&nbsp;J s</mtext></mrow></math> ]",
